Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:23:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] TEACH-ZALLUP (web): Teach -- In Z All Up / Out Z All Up
 (golden uteach.cpp:4466 / :4480) and the Index tab's btnZ1Servo / btnZ2Servo
 / btnArm1YServo / btnArm2YServo (golden :4253 / :4270 / :2919) are wired;
 they were on the page with no handler

* page/ht9045_teach_zallup_c.js (new): binds the 6 buttons through HTMotorAccess.send. Z All Up shows "Homeing..." until the
  runtime's motion.homeJob clears (back at once if C++ refuses); the Servo captions follow state.servoOn; the control token is
  kept while a Z homes; no confirm dialog (golden has none). If the catalog lacks the rows the buttons are greyed with a reason.
* JSON/motor-access.json + JSON/js/motor-access.js (file:// copy, identical): six uteach rows -- btnIn/OutZAllUp -> teachZAllUp
  (kind motion), the four Servo buttons -> teachIndexServo (kind control). C++ side: machine commit 77a1741.
* page/HW.teach.html: the one <script> line, and the TEACH-UNWIRED-2 note says they are wired now.

Verified: inline scripts + the new file syntax OK, JSON parses; ctest WebMotorAccess (reads this JSON) / WebCmdGuard /
TeachButtonsGen / WebTeachLeave / GaliRouteEngine / GaliRouteLive 6/6 passed; production_audit 0 changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
